College Portal: Master PRD and Build Prompts
For Google AI Studio (Build mode), free tech stack, role-based, security-first
1. How to use this document
Sections 2 to 9 are the Master PRD. It is the single source of truth for what you are building. Sections 10 to 13 contain the prompts you paste into Google AI Studio, in order, along with the Vibe Coding Checklist applied to this project.
The rule that keeps the build clean: never paste everything at once. Paste the PRD summary once (Prompt 0), ask for a plan (Prompt 1), review the plan, and only then build one module per prompt. Each prompt is small enough that you can review the result before moving on.
2. Product overview
Product name: Campus Portal (rename freely)
One-line vision: One secure place where students, parents, faculty, and the college office handle attendance, results, fees, notices, mentoring, and leave, with every person seeing only what their role allows.
Problems it solves
• Attendance is kept on paper or scattered spreadsheets, and students find out about shortages too late.
• Fee dues, receipts, and deadlines are communicated by word of mouth or noticeboards.
• Leave requests move through physical letters with no status tracking.
• Students do not know who their mentor is, what their subjects are, or who teaches them.
• Parents have no reliable view of attendance, marks, and dues.
Goals
• Every role has a purpose-built dashboard with the three or four things that role needs daily.
• Attendance, fees, and leave each follow a clear workflow with status and history.
• Notices reach exactly the right audience (college, department, class, or individual).
• Data is protected by row-level access rules, not just hidden buttons.
• The interface looks like a considered, editorial product rather than a generated template.
Non-goals for version 1
• Live payment collection with real money (use test mode or manual payment recording first).
• Native mobile apps (build a responsive web app that can be installed as a PWA).
• Online exams and video classes.
Success metrics
• A faculty member can mark attendance for a class of 60 in under 60 seconds.
• A student can apply for leave in under 45 seconds and see the approval status without asking anyone.
• Zero cross-role data leaks in the security test (Section 12).
• Lighthouse scores of 90 or above for performance, accessibility, and best practices on the landing page.
