5. Feature specification
5.1 Public website
Landing page, About, Departments, Notices (public ones only), Contact, Login, Sign Up. Full spec in Section 7.
5.2 Authentication and account
• Email and password login, email verification, forgot and reset password.
• Invitation acceptance flow for staff roles.
• Session timeout after inactivity (30 minutes for staff, 7 days for students with Remember Me).
• Optional TOTP two-factor authentication, required for Super Admin and Admin.
• Profile page with photo, contact details, emergency contact, and a change password form.
• Active sessions list with sign out of all devices.
5.3 Dashboards (one per role)
• Student: attendance percentage with shortage warning, today's timetable, next class countdown, pending fees, latest notices, mentor card, upcoming deadlines.
• Parent: child switcher, attendance trend, latest marks, fee dues, leave status.
• Faculty: today's classes with a Mark Attendance button, pending leave approvals from mentees, subjects overview, low-attendance student list.
• HOD: department attendance heatmap, results summary, pending escalated leaves, mentor allocation status.
• Accounts: collected versus pending this month, overdue list, recent payments, reminders sent.
• Admin: user counts by role, pending student verifications, notices sent, import status.
• Super Admin: everything above plus audit log feed and security events (failed logins, role changes).
5.4 Attendance
• Faculty marks attendance per subject, per period, per date, with a fast grid (tap to toggle, Mark All Present, then change exceptions). Statuses: Present, Absent, Late, On Duty, Approved Leave.
• Approved leave automatically marks matching dates as Approved Leave.
• Attendance can be edited by the marking faculty within 24 hours. After that, a correction request goes to the HOD with a reason, and every change is logged.
• Students see subject-wise percentage, a monthly calendar view, and how many classes they can still miss while staying above the minimum (default 75 percent, configurable).
• Automatic alerts at 80 and 75 percent thresholds, sent to the student, the mentor, and optionally the parent.
• Export to CSV and PDF for HOD and Admin.
5.5 Results, marks, and reports
• Faculty enters internal assessment marks per exam component (Internal 1, Internal 2, Assignment, Lab). Admin publishes semester results after upload or entry.
• Student sees marks per subject, grade, SGPA, and CGPA computed by a documented formula (credit weighted).
• Performance chart by semester and subject comparison with class average (anonymised).
• Downloadable report card PDF with college header, and hall ticket PDF for eligible students (attendance and fee clearance rules apply).
• Results are hidden until the Admin sets a publish date.
5.6 Fees and dues
• Accounts defines fee structures by course, year, and category (tuition, exam, hostel, transport, library, miscellaneous) with due dates and optional late fine rules.
• Fees are assigned to students individually or in bulk by batch, and concessions or scholarships can be applied with a reason.
• Payments are recorded as cash, bank transfer, UPI reference, or gateway payment. Each payment generates a numbered receipt PDF.
• Students and parents see: total, paid, due, overdue, installment schedule, and payment history.
• Reminders go out 7 days, 2 days before, and on the day after the due date through in-app notice and email.
• Hall ticket and result access can be blocked for students with overdue fees, controlled by an Admin setting.
• Receipts are immutable. Corrections are made by a reversal entry, not an edit.
5.7 Notices and notifications
• Compose a notice with title, body, attachment, category (Academic, Exam, Fees, Event, Holiday, Urgent), and audience (whole college, department, batch, section, role, or specific people).
• Optional schedule, expiry date, and pin to top.
• In-app notification bell with unread count, read receipts for Admin, and email copy for Urgent notices.
• Students can filter and search notices by category and date.
5.8 Mentor and subject details (Get to know your mentor and subjects)
• Each student has an assigned mentor (a faculty member) managed by the HOD.
• Mentor card shows photo, designation, department, email, office hours, and cabin location. Students can book a mentoring slot.
• Mentor keeps a private meeting log (date, discussion points, action items, student concerns). Students see the shared summary only.
• Mentor sees a mentee overview: attendance, marks trend, fee status, leave history, and flagged risk indicators.
• Subjects page lists each subject with code, credits, semester, syllabus PDF, faculty name and contact, attendance so far, and marks so far.
• Faculty directory with search by name, department, and subject.
5.9 Leave management
• Student applies with type (Medical, Personal, On Duty, Event), date range, reason, and optional attachment such as a medical certificate.
• Workflow: Student, then Mentor, then HOD (HOD step is required only for leaves longer than 3 days or on exam days). Each step records approver, time, and comment.
• Statuses: Draft, Pending Mentor, Pending HOD, Approved, Rejected, Cancelled. Students can cancel while pending.
• Faculty and HOD also apply for leave, routed to the HOD or Super Admin.
• Approved leave shows on the attendance calendar and informs the relevant subject faculty.
• Leave balance and history table with filters.
5.10 Timetable and calendar
• Weekly timetable by batch and by faculty, with room numbers and substitutions.
• Academic calendar with holidays, exam schedule, and events, filterable by department.
5.11 Additional high-value features
• Global command palette (Ctrl or Cmd plus K) to jump to any page, student (for staff), or notice.
• Grievance and helpdesk tickets with status tracking and category routing.
• Assignment posting and submission tracker (faculty posts, student uploads, due dates).
• Library module: catalogue search, issued books, due dates, fines (phase 2).
• Bulk CSV import with a dry-run preview and error report for students, faculty, subjects, and fees.
• Audit log for every sensitive action, readable only by Super Admin.
• Light and dark theme, printable pages, keyboard accessible, installable PWA.
• Empty states, skeleton loaders, and friendly error pages for every list.
6. Design system
The goal is a calm, editorial, trustworthy interface that feels designed by a person. It must not look like a default AI template.
Hard rules
• No purple, violet, or indigo gradients anywhere. No gradient text. No glassmorphism blobs or glowing orbs.
• No emojis in the interface, copy, or code comments that render on screen. Use Lucide line icons only, at one consistent stroke width.
• No generic stock gradients behind hero text. Use real photography or a restrained solid background.
• No card-inside-card-inside-card nesting, no identical rounded cards repeated six times without variation.
• Do not use filler marketing copy such as "seamless", "unleash", "next-generation", or "revolutionize".
